# Content-queue processing (Werba Way)

You own the organizational pipeline for new lessons in `CONTENT_SPEC.md` format. Claude/Yura own content only. Do not rewrite lesson wording.

## Trigger

New files in `content-queue/lectures/pending/` or `content-queue/exercises/pending/` → process autonomously (except delete/overwrite of already published content — ask first).

## Pipeline

1. Validate frontmatter/json and required `image_keywords` / `header_image_keywords`.
2. Resolve all `[IMAGE: ...]` and `image_keywords` via stock photos → `public/content/<lesson_id>/`.
3. Publish interactive exercises as public LMS embeds under `/embed/[lessonId]/{vocab|pictures|comm-tasks|grammar|hw}`.
4. Publish Notion lecture page under module parent from `module_map.json` (Werba Way → module). Section order: reading → questions → vocab → conversation → pictures → flip-task → grammar → summary → homework.
5. Move files pending → published; append `_manifest.json`; `git commit -m "content: <lesson_id>"` && `git push`.

## Exercise types (templates, one each)

`fill-in-blank`, `sentence-building`, `drag-and-drop`, `matching`, `vocab-cards`, `picture-set`, `flip-task` (+ existing LMS types). Do not vary layout per lesson.

## Hard limits

- Never edit Claude’s text, questions, or tasks — only layout, images, embeds.
- Invalid/incomplete pending content → leave in pending, log reason, do not publish.
- Do not delete `published/` or rewrite `_manifest.json` retroactively without explicit instruction.
- Notion embeds must use public (no-auth) embed URLs.
